model_comparison.m3_matched_complexity.reason:
M3 is a panel of five fixed, disclosed bases with the same spline/Box-Cox form and 16 parameters as M2:
- opponent (L−M, S−(L+M), L+M);
- linear sRGB (IEC primaries);
- CIE RGB (700/546.1/435.8 nm);
- CIELAB on its own (ΔL*, Δa*, Δb*);
- LCh on (ΔL*, ΔC*, ΔH*) with the standard ΔH* = 2√(C1C2) sin(Δh/2).

Every axis of every basis is rescaled to unit RMS over the training design. None is a fitted rotation, and there is no per-stimulus linearization.

