identifiability.gauge_fixed.reason:
The gauge is fixed in advance and disclosed:
- outer f is one-parameter Box-Cox with f(0)=0 and f'(0)=1;
- inner g_k are monotone PCHIP with g_k(0)=0, carrying all flexible shape;
- the scale gauge is Σ_k g_k(r_k)=1 at r_k=1 after unit-RMS standardization.

The code implements this through the S1 normalization, and tests confirm that M2 with linear inner functions equals M1.

identifiability.collinearity_quantified.reason:
The paper quantifies the design's collinearity in three ways:
- variance on the top two singular directions of the pair-difference matrices: 99.78% (Helm), 100.00% (Ekman);
- minimum cone ridge separation in the spanned plane: 6.3° [4.3, 8.0] (Helm) and 3.0° [2.9, 3.1] (Ekman);
- the |ΔL| vs |ΔM| scatter (Fig. 2b).

The logs add corr(ΔL, ΔM) of −0.63 and 0.38 and condition numbers of 21.2 (Helm), 348.2 (Ekman) and 341.4 (pooled chromatic).

identifiability.synthetic_recovery.reason:
Recovery of distinct curves:
- 200 seeded synthetic datasets at the real design and fitted noise, with distinct f_L, f_M, f_S (x^0.35, x^1, x^0.6);
- per-curve error with intervals: f_L 0.022 [0.004, 0.078], f_M 0.034, f_S 0.026;
- 95% recovery bands and band widths are logged;
- the L–M contrast is recovered with the correct sign 100% of the time, and distances correlate 0.9994 with truth.

M2-vs-M3 discrimination:
- power simulations under every basis show 94% correct basis under the opponent generator;
- the delta for each generator is reported with intervals.

What is weakly resolvable is also quantified: K2-cone vs K2-opponent at 80% with CI [−0.012, +0.035], and the realistic fitted cone effect at +0.040 [−0.012, +0.086].

Weaknesses:
- recoverability of individual curves is shown only for a deliberately strong generator;
- failure item (1) contradicts the recovery result.

identifiability.m2_m3_discrimination_ass.reason:
Discrimination between M3- and M2-generated data was simulated at the real design:
- under the nearest (opponent) generator, the correct basis wins 94% and M2−best M3 = −0.051 [−0.112, −0.006];
